-- title:
--   Reciprocity between end leading residues and branch norms of V
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a discrete valuation domain that is adically complete for its maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible and $e \ge 1$, and write $R =$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)`, the quotient of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^e$. Let $x \in R$ be nonzero and let $ab = (a,b)$ be a pair of one-variable power series over $W$ with $b$ of zero constant term such that $x$ is the class of `inU a + inV b`, i.e. of $a(X_0) + b(X_1)$; assume some coefficient of $a$ is a unit, and that either the constant coefficient of $a$ is a unit or some coefficient $b_j$ with $j \ge 1$ is a unit. Write $\mathrm{nfCoeff}$ for the $\mathbb{Z}$-indexed normal-form coefficients of $ab$ ($n \ge 0 \mapsto a_n$, $-(j+1) \mapsto b_{j+1}$), and for $t \in \{0,e\}$ let $D_t$ be the set of $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ whose term order `termOrder (IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal W) e t ab n`, namely the valuation of $\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,n$ plus `annulusWeight e t (nfExponent n)`, attains the representative Gauss order `repGaussOrder (IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal W) e t (inU a + inV b)`, the infimum over multidegrees $d$ of the valuation of the coefficient at $d$ plus `annulusWeight e t d`. Here `leadingResidue ϖ c` is $0$ for $c = 0$ and otherwise the residue in the residue field of $W$ of the unit part `unitPart ϖ c` of $c$. Then, with the product taken (in the sense of `finprod`) over the prime ideals $Q$ of $R$ with $Q \ne 0$, $Q$ not containing the constant $\varpi$, and $x \in Q$, $$\mathrm{leadingResidue}_\varpi\big(\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,(\sup D_e)\big) \cdot \prod_Q \overline{\mathrm{unitPart}_\varpi\big(N_{W}(\,\overline{V}\bmod Q\,)\big)}^{\,\ell_Q} = (-1)^{(\inf D_0 - \sup D_e)^+}\,\mathrm{leadingResidue}_\varpi\big(\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,(\inf D_0)\big),$$ where $\overline{V}$ is the element `V (ϖ ^ e)`, the class of the second variable (so $U \cdot V$ is the constant $\varpi^e$), $N_W$ is the algebra norm of $R/Q$ over $W$, and $\ell_Q$ is the `toNat` of the length of the localisation of $R/xR$ at $Q$ over the local ring of $R$ at $Q$.
--
--   This is the reciprocity, on the Deligne–Rapoport crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi^e)$, between the leading residues of an element at its two ends and the unit parts of the norms of $\overline{V}$ along the horizontal primes through it, here under the hypothesis that the normal form of $x$ has a unit coefficient on each branch. It is obtained by evaluating the $W$-norm of $\overline{V}$ on the free quotient $R/xR$ in two ways, through the branch decomposition of the norm and through the relation $U \cdot V = \varpi^e$, and is used to derive the corresponding identity for an arbitrary nonzero $x$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_leadingResidue_nfCoeff_sSup_mul_finprod_residue_unitPart_norm_pow_eq_of_isUnit_coeff.lean

